e":"text_delta","text":" why lookups"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" are very"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" fast, typ"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ically \""},{"type":"text_delta","text":"constant time\", no matter how"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" many"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" items"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" you have.\n\n## What if"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" two keys land"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" in the same slot?\n\nThis"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" is called a **collision**."},{"type":"text_delta","text":" It's"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" unavoidable, because"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" there are far"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" more poss"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ible keys than sl"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ots. Say"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" \"Car"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ol\" also"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" hashes to 3. There"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" are two common f"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ixes:\n\n- **Ch"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"aining:** each"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" slot hol"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ds a small list"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"."},{"type":"text_delta","text":" Slot 3 hol"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ds both"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" Alice and Carol, and"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" you"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" check"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" the ke"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ys in"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" that short"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" list to find the right one."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n- **Open addressing:"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"** if slot 3 is"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" taken, try slot 4"},{"type":"text_delta","text":", then "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"5, and so on until"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" you find an"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" empty one.\n\n## What if"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" it"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" gets too"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" full?\n\nIf"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" too"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" many items are cr"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ammed in"},{"type":"text_delta","text":", coll"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"isions p"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ile up and lookups sl"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ow down. So"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" when"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" the map gets about"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" 70"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"% full, it"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" cre"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ates a b"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"igger array and re"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-places every item using"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" the"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" new size"},{"type":"text_delta","text":". This is called **resizing"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"**"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" (or r"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ehashing).\n\n## In"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" code\n\n```python\nph"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"one"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"_num"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"bers = {}                "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"  # a h"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ash map (a"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" \""},{"type":"text_delta","text":"dict\" in Python)"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\nphone_numbers[\""},{"type":"text_delta","text":"Alice\"] = \"555-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"1234\""},{"type":"text_delta","text":" # put\nphone_numb"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ers[\"Bob\"] ="},{"type":"text_delta","text":" \"555-9876\""},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nprint(phone_numbers"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"[\"Alice\"])       "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"# get"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" -> "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"555-1234\n```"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nOther languages use"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" different"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" names for"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" it"},{"type":"text_delta","text":": `H"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ashMap` in Java,"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" `Map` or"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" object"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" in JavaScript, `"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"unordered_map` in C"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"++."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n## Key"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" takeaways\n\n- A"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" hash function conver"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ts a key into an"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" array position"},{"type":"text_delta","text":".\n- L"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ookups,"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" inserts,"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" and deletes are us"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ually very"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" fast ("},{"type":"text_delta","text":"average O"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"(1)).\n- Coll"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"isions are handled by cha"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ining or prob"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ing.\n- Keys must"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" be unique."},{"type":"text_delta","text":" Stor"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ing a new value under an"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" existing key over"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"writes the"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" old one.\n- Items are"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" gener"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ally not st"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ored in a me"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"aningful order."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A hash map stores **key → value** pairs and lets you find a value quickly by its key. It works like a coat check at a theater.\n\n## The problem it solves\n\nSay you want to store people's phone numbers:\n\n- \"Alice\" → 555-1234\n- \"Bob\" → 555-9876\n\nYou could keep them in a list and scan from the start until you find \"Bob\". With 1 million entries, that scan is slow. A hash map jumps straight to the right spot instead.\n\n## The three pieces\n\n**1. An array of slots (buckets).** Picture a row of numbered mailboxes, 0 to 7, for example.\n\n**2. A hash function.** This turns any key into a number. For example, \"Alice\" might become 3 and \"Bob\" might become 6. The same key always gives the same number. A simplified version might add up the letter codes and take the remainder after dividing by the number of slots.\n\n**3. Storing and retrieving.**\n- **Put(\"Alice\", 555-1234):** run the hash function on \"Alice\" to get 3, then put the value in slot 3.\n- **Get(\"Alice\"):** run the hash function again to get 3, then look in slot 3 and return the value.\n\nThere's no searching. You compute the slot and go straight to it. That's why lookups are very fast, typically \"constant time\", no matter how many items you have.\n\n## What if two keys land in the same slot?\n\nThis is called a **collision**. It's unavoidable, because there are far more possible keys than slots. Say \"Carol\" also hashes to 3. There are two common fixes:\n\n- **Chaining:** each slot holds a small list. Slot 3 holds both Alice and Carol, and you check the keys in that short list to find the right one.\n- **Open addressing:** if slot 3 is taken, try slot 4, then 5, and so on until you find an empty one.\n\n## What if it gets too full?\n\nIf too many items are crammed in, collisions pile up and lookups slow down. So when the map gets about 70% full, it creates a bigger array and re-places every item using the new size. This is called **resizing** (or rehashing).\n\n## In code\n\n```python\nphone_numbers = {}                  # a hash map (a \"dict\" in Python)\nphone_numbers[\"Alice\"] = \"555-1234\" # put\nphone_numbers[\"Bob\"] = \"555-9876\"\n\nprint(phone_numbers[\"Alice\"])       # get -> 555-1234\n```\n\nOther languages use different names for it: `HashMap` in Java, `Map` or object in JavaScript, `unordered_map` in C++.\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n- A hash function converts a key into an array position.\n- Lookups, inserts, and deletes are usually very fast (average O(1)).\n- Collisions are handled by chaining or probing.\n- Keys must be unique. Storing a new value under an existing key overwrites the old one.\n- Items are generally not stored in a meaningful order."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":4517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
